4.2 — `revert-check` on the widened-fetch rule (change `poi-name-filter`, design D3; spec
`poi-search` — A filtered search asks for a candidate set, not a page). Taken by hand in
`.pi/worktrees/archive-875`, branch `archive/poi-name-filter`, on the tree whose cases 4.1
records green.

The rule under mutation: the POI walk is asked for `POI_CANDIDATE_CAP` (2000) exactly when a
name filter is in effect, and for the display limit (`MapCanvasViewModel.MAX_POI_RESULTS`,
100) otherwise. Mutated to fetch the display limit under the filter as well — the fetch width
at the client call, so the walk is still *recorded* as the widened one and the case fails on
its assertion rather than on a state that never arrives.

Mutation (single site, `app/src/main/java/com/naviveylin/ui/map/MapCanvasViewModelSearch.kt`,
`MapCanvasViewModel.searchPoisOnce`, the width handed to the native walk):

    -                    typeNames, lat, lon, radiusMeters, poiRequestWidth, generation
    +                    typeNames, lat, lon, radiusMeters,
    +                    minOf(poiRequestWidth, MapCanvasViewModel.MAX_POI_RESULTS), generation

