Note on the mutation site. The rule has two expressions: `poiRequestWidthFor(filter)` (the
search button's width) and the widen path's own `poiRequestWidth = POI_CANDIDATE_CAP`. Mutating
either of those alone leaves the case's `poiWidened` wait unsatisfied under a different
mechanism — mutating the widen path's assignment makes the case hang until `runTest`'s
one-minute timeout instead of asserting — so the mutation is placed where the width actually
reaches the walk. One rule, one mutation, one red case.